[1m[38;5;231mWhat should this identifier actually represent?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mAnonymous visitor ID (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mGenerated client-side on first visit, persists indefinitely, same before and after login. Works for every form [39m
     [38;5;246mtoday with no backend. Identifies a browser, not a person.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Per-session ID
     [38;5;246mNew ID each visit, dies with the browser session. Lightest privacy footprint, but no correlation across visits.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Authenticated user ID
     [38;5;246mIssued by the server on successful login. Truly identifies the person, but requires a real auth response contract [39m
     [38;5;246mand is unavailable to pre-login forms.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m Anonymous + linked user ID
     [38;5;246mAnonymous ID always present, associated with the real user ID once authenticated. Most capable, most machinery: two
[39m     [38;5;246midentifiers plus linking rules.[39m
